  "note": "23 subtopics, above the usual 4-15, because this chapter carries two book parts (I. Amines, II. Diazonium Salts) with ten numbered headings, and sections 9.4 and 9.6 are themselves lists of individually named and numbered methods/reactions (Gabriel phthalimide synthesis, Hoffmann bromamide degradation, carbylamine reaction, Hinsberg's reagent, Sandmeyer/Gattermann) that NEET tests one at a time; folding them together would make one subtopic absorb most of the chapter. Hard placements: P16 (Intext 9.1, classify amines) sits physically after 9.3 Nomenclature but asks about classification, so it is under 9.2; P119, P121, P123, P125 are end-of-chapter exercises that span several subtopics and were each put with their first/dominant item (P119 and P124 descent-of-series conversions under Hoffmann bromamide; P121 short notes under carbylamine reaction; P123 and P125 reaction-sequence questions under 9.10 synthesis, the least certain of these); P116 and P120 (chemical tests to distinguish 1/2/3 amines) go with Hinsberg's reagent though the carbylamine test also applies; P114 (chapter Summary) and P129-P131 (Answers to Some Intext Questions, two of them bare equations) are chapter-wide and were placed with the chapter-opening definition and with 9.10 respectively. I found no short cluster that reads as content migrated in from a removed chapter; the 9.6 and 9.9 reaction lists and the diazonium part all sit naturally under their own headings. Headings list contains duplicate numbers 9.5, 9.7, 9.8, 9.9 because the exercise prompts were captured as headings; from_heading values above use the section headings, not those exercise lines, and 'I. AMINES' / 'II. DIAZONIUM SALTS' are in-text part headings not present in the headings list."
}
